  199:     computed the same todo list, and re-fetched the same 427 papers while both
  200:     appending to one ledger. `ps` on Git Bash shows no command arguments, so
  201:     grepping for the script name reported 0 matches and hid it. A lock makes the
  202:     second instance fail loudly instead of silently doubling the NCBI load.
  203: 
  204:     STALE-LOCK RECOVERY, and this one is load-bearing for the standing run: a
  205:     KILLED harvester leaves its lock behind. A watchdog that restarts this lane
  206:     from checkpoint would then hit the lock, fail, and the lane would stay dead
  207:     for good â€” a permanent outage caused by the safety mechanism. Verified live:
  208:     killing a harvester mid-flight left `.fulltext_linked_rct.pc1.lock` orphaned.
  209:     So we record the PID and take the lock if its owner is gone. A lock held by a
  210:     LIVE process is still refused â€” that is the case it exists for.
  211:     """
  212:     lock = os.path.join(C.DATA, f".fulltext_{corpus}.{C.NODE}.lock")
  213:     for attempt in (1, 2):
  214:         try:
  215:             fd = os.open(lock, os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_WRONLY)
